# Shell scripts get baked into Docker images and run there — a CRLF shebang
# ("#!/bin/sh\r") fails with "not found" because the container looks for an
# interpreter literally named "/bin/sh\r". Windows' default core.autocrlf
# normalises them back to CRLF on every checkout/stash without this, which
# already broke the frontend container's entrypoint twice in one session.
*.sh text eol=lf
